{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords","id":1369936,"title":"What unique weaknesses did you give your Deathlords???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-23T17:43:47-08:00","id":1369936,"title":"What unique weaknesses did you give your Deathlords???","content":"I have always found the option that Deathlords can each have secret weaknesses that can kill them permanently interesting.<br /> <br /> What unique weaknesses did you give to the Deathlords in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T17:59:53-08:00","id":1369937,"title":"","content":"I gave my Deathlords the paired secret weaknesses that having been a living Solar means absolutely nothing about your powers as a ghost and that the Neverborn are pretty much useless as a source of anything but insanity. My Deathlords are highly-motivated and highly-skilled ghosts who found and seized opportunity when it became available to them, which also explains why they were so interested in this whole &quot;Our own Exalted&quot; business. <br /> Of course, they lie their asses off about this, which is where the &quot;secret weakness&quot; rumors come from. Very, very elaborate lies, often involving other Deathlords, visiting Exalted, or spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T19:00:04-08:00","id":1369947,"title":"","content":"In the one game where it mattered for me, the Deathlords could only be kill by the current bearer of their former exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:49:04-08:00","id":1370140,"title":"","content":"The weakness I found least interesting was &quot;go fetch this magic rock... because&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters being struck down by his last living descendant was one. I can't recall which Deathlords but we convinced one to voluntarily enter Lethe by getting them to love a baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T02:44:18-08:00","id":1370279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370140#post1370140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mask of Winters being struck down by his last living descendant was one. I can't recall which Deathlords but we convinced one to voluntarily enter Lethe by getting them to love a baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>These both sound like they have some interesting backstories. How did your group convince a Deathlord to love a baby?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:06:39-08:00","id":1370296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370279#post1370279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These both sound like they have some interesting backstories. How did your group convince a Deathlord to love a baby?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly? Social Charms.<br /> <br /> I think we were up against The First Forsaken Lion so step one was removing The Princess Magnificent With Lips Of Coral And Robes Of Black Feathers. We decided the best way to do that was winning her love to provide the hilt to wield her hatred for the Lion as an effective blade. Which sort of, accidently, led to having her defend a baby from He Who Holds In Thrall (and having her go into Lethe). But possibly it was from a game against the Lover... this is a decade ago.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters had literally thousands of descendants in that game. To start with. We totally Macbeth'ed him with a prophecy that he would be struct down by one of his living descendants, which caused him to go on a genocidal spree -- uniting the Realm and the Riverprovinces against him. The Mask managed to kill all his descendants bar one (a PC Sidereal of Endings) in a &quot;Just As Planned&quot;/&quot;You played yourself&quot; moment of greatness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T06:11:00-08:00","id":1370335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1369947#post1369947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the one game where it mattered for me, the Deathlords could only be kill by the current bearer of their former exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did this. Then the PC who was the current bearer of Walker in Darkness (the big bad of that campaign)'s Exaltation was accidentally killed by another PC in a fight against Sidereals. And I realised that making one PC the chosen one is a risky strategy. Would not do again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:44:30-08:00","id":1370353,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never personally had cause to use any but I can think of some.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed in the light of a harvest moon.<br /> <br /> Deathlord split them self into several different personalities, they can all resurrect eachother so you have to make them all destroyed at once.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be slain by some other ghost passing on, and dragging their soul to Lethe with them.<br /> <br /> Deathlord must be convinced to let go of Creation and pass on willingly.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed by a trusted ally betraying them.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can\u2019t be killed but can be permanently trapped in a specific hearthstone.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be destroyed by immolation in an occult ceremony.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed by their own attacks.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed by somebody they have a defining tie of love for, or has one for them.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed by first binding their soul to living flesh and then slaying that. Debatably breaking the resurrection rule.<br /> <br /> Deathlord can only be killed by wrestling them into their original tomb and crossing the lid with a seal of the Maiden of Endings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:49:39-08:00","id":1370355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370353#post1370353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlord split them self into several different personalities, they can all resurrect eachother so you have to make them all destroyed at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, convince one or more of them to <i>not want</i> to resurrect the others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T08:46:13-08:00","id":1370365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370355#post1370355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, convince one or more of them to <i>not want</i> to resurrect the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s be good. You could even have a bunch of different answers to their various forms. The unreasonable rage monster needs to die, the spiteful but pathetic one can just be locked in a prison with salt lines, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:01:05-08:00","id":1370370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370140#post1370140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weakness I found least interesting was &quot;go fetch this magic rock... because&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a meta level the Hungry Stone was sort of perfect. It highlighted how Island Five had utterly taken over The Silver Prince's portrayal to the point he was The First and Forsaken Lion but with an unstoppable navy instead of an army. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:29:34-08:00","id":1370375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370370#post1370370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a meta level the Hungry Stone was sort of perfect. It highlighted how Island Five had utterly taken over The Silver Prince's portrayal to the point he was The First and Forsaken Lion but with an unstoppable navy instead of an army. </div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on this? I\u2019m not super familiar with the silver prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:37:53-08:00","id":1370376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370375#post1370375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you elaborate on this? I\u2019m not super familiar with the silver prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hungry Stone is something on Island Five which draws in the souls of Skullstone's population when they die so they can be soulforged into the Doom Fleet. Which kind of makes all his politics and the culture he's built and the core of his original goal and characterisation just a big lie to distract people from the secret construction of said fleet.<br /> <br /> In RotSE destroying the stone or incorporating it into a weapon is an easy way to literally hurt the Silver Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T20:38:46-08:00","id":1370499,"title":"","content":"Long, long ago, in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/46387-dex-davican-s-deathlord\">another reality</a>...<br /> <br /> (Edit: Few to none of these are likely to fit Ex3 Deathlords, if &quot;truly unkillable without a secret weakness&quot; will even still be a thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:03:25-08:00","id":1370546,"title":"","content":"The biggest one we had come up in our game was for The Lover Clad in a Raiment of Tears. Her secret weakness was being killed by someone who truly loved her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:43:20-08:00","id":1370669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370499#post1370499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long, long ago, in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/46387-dex-davican-s-deathlord\">another reality</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang, that is some beautiful stuff.<br /> <br /> So... have you had a chance to write up Harbinger of Lost Hope?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T20:27:00-08:00","id":1370691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370669#post1370669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dang, that is some beautiful stuff.<br /> <br /> So... have you had a chance to write up Harbinger of Lost Hope?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, my game went on indefinite hiatus not long after I wrote these. Burned out on maintaining a game with 2E mechanics, and my group never found a replacement system that worked for everyone. (Our Dawn player didn't like Ex3's combat.)<br /> <br /> But Exalted: Essence has me hopeful for a return at some point.<br /> <br /> Edit: And thank you for the compliment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 02-26-2020, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T20:52:48-08:00","id":1370695,"title":"","content":"I'm frequently going to go with death by epiphany, something that strikes at the hearth of a Deathlord's being and leaves them unable to go on being. But in the instances where the Deathlords fell, those were done by NPC's, while the heroes had their own victories elsewhere.<br /> <br /> There were maybe three times a Deathlord died--or could have--in the game I ran for several years:<br /> <br /> 1.) The Mask of Winters didn't show up, but could theoretically have been obliterated by the destruction of Juggernaut which a couple of NPC's did (the players weren't involved at all in Thorns, so this was something they stumbled upon rather than NPC's stealing their thunder). But that was a sort of extreme overkill brute-force solution which left the surrounding Underworld a scarred wreck shredding unprotected souls into Lethe. (EDIT 6.5 years later) This was also the culmination of a prophecy, that all who desired his fall would be known to him, and none that desired his power could take it. The teamwork of a young warrior who just wanted to avenge the executed queen and a genuinely, frighteningly mad sorceress who saw the whole thing as a fascinating exercise in science neatly circumvented this. Askatu inherited responsibility for Thorns (which he never wanted), and the Mask didn't notice Mint--who was pathologically incapable of malice or mercy--until she staked him to the back of Juggernaut with a staff she used as the focus for a casting of Benediction of Archgenesis<br /> <br /> 2.) The Silver Prince in my game was legitimately a double-triple-decatuple-googolplex-agent Deathlord who was either making the fleet that would destroy the world or making a fleet that would be seized from him and wielded by whoever defeated him against the Neverborn. Much like the Green Lady, he wasn't exactly sure which side he was on, but if confronted with incontrovertible proof that he was ultimately acting in Creation's best interest, then it would have unmade him. This never actually happened, and eventually if not stopped he absolutely would have taken to the seas and killed everything he found.<br /> <br /> 3.) One homebrew Deathlord, the Ashen-Winged Skald, had despaired in life of a Creation without himself, and had set plans in motion that would ultimately overwrite whoever inherited his exaltation with his own personality and experiences. In the Usurpation, he survived not only long enough to realize that he would not go out on his own terms, but that the Exaltations of his fellow Lawgivers were not returning. Accepting the offer of the Neverborn was a given. But Fate has a funny way of seeing things through, and in the twilight days of the Second Age his Exaltation returned, finding a young man whose family had passed down the trapped trappings of the predecessor. What happened next was not fast, nor a happy story, but the ancient lawgiver's plans came to fruition. In a later season, when he confronted his ancient and restless shade, the epiphany alone shattered the Skald's raison d'etre. Perhaps in some other time this might not have been enough--it was not that long ago that the Deathlord had been at ground zero of a disaster that reshaped a pole of Creation and the heavens above it--but the mere recognizance of Athyfer Returned was enough to unmake him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-12-2026, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:16:58-08:00","id":1370799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370499#post1370499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Edit: Few to none of these are likely to fit Ex3 Deathlords, if &quot;truly unkillable without a secret weakness&quot; will even still be a thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the fact they can come back after being seemingly destroyed is the most interesting thing about them. It's just not been realised in the previous editions due to treating them as essence 10 endgame bosses that you might as well kill forever to make things narratively satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T21:07:58-08:00","id":1370934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370799#post1370799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think the fact they can come back after being seemingly destroyed is the most interesting thing about them. It's just not been realised in the previous editions due to treating them as essence 10 endgame bosses that you might as well kill forever to make things narratively satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a thought-provoking point. A villain that you have to seriously consider coexistence with\u2014because the alternative is killing them over and over, forever\u2014contributes to Exalted\u2019s thematic exploration of the consequences of violence. But does it do so in a way that Celestial Exaltations don\u2019t already do in a more interesting fashion? Hmm.<br /> <br /> ...sorry, off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T21:42:09-08:00","id":1370937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370934#post1370934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a thought-provoking point. A villain that you have to seriously consider coexistence with\u2014because the alternative is killing them over and over, forever\u2014contributes to Exalted\u2019s thematic exploration of the consequences of violence. But does it do so in a way that Celestial Exaltations don\u2019t already do in a more interesting fashion? Hmm.<br /> <br /> ...sorry, off-topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say so. Unless you're an Exalt allied with the Wyld Hunt, where the issue isn't who the Celestial Exalt or what they have done so much as what they are and you're more or less signed onto an endless war on them for nothing more or less than that, killing a Celestial Exalt does effectively get rid of that person unless they leave behind a ghost. Their successor isn't inherently antagonistic towards you, and may not know or care of your existence.<br /> <br /> The Deathlord absolutely does have a level of continuity of existence, personality, and purpose that the legacy of an Exaltation lacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:31:14-08:00","id":1370976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1370934#post1370934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a thought-provoking point. A villain that you have to seriously consider coexistence with\u2014because the alternative is killing them over and over, forever\u2014contributes to Exalted\u2019s thematic exploration of the consequences of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dormammu! I'm here to bargain!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:53:07-08:00","id":1370979,"title":"","content":"Abyssals had a charm to pass a negative intimacy towards their successor last edition. The problem is that such an ability stems from &quot;I hate you so much even my successor will hate you!&quot; which is a pretty clear indicator that you can't co-exist with this person and should take your chances with the person whose never met you, has to start again from essence 1 and might be a pretty reasonable person outside of this predecessor imposed hatred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:36:15-08:00","id":1372018,"title":"","content":"Since Deathlord in third edition won\u2019t be invincible NPC that can win against your whole circle, so the whole thing about super secret weakness has lost much of its bite for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T19:10:14-08:00","id":1372081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1372018#post1372018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Deathlord in third edition won\u2019t be invincible NPC that can win against your whole circle, so the whole thing about super secret weakness has lost much of its bite for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring broken Elder Charms from the 1st release of Dreams of the First Age, I thought Deathlords were epic but approachable antagonists in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> If I understood them correctly, they were intelligent &amp; cunning antagonists whom can learn from past defeats, had massive resources, &amp; not the type you want to fight more than once. I thought that gave a secret weakness that can kept them defeated a distinct appeal, regardless if you curb stomped them once or not.<br /> <br /> I honestly can not think of any antagonists in 2nd Edition that could definitively defeat a Solar Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 02-29-2020, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T08:08:50-08:00","id":1372155,"title":"","content":"Not my game, but I do recall my sister\u2019s 2nd edition game had the Mask of Winters\u2019 weakness being Juggernaut\u2019s hungry ghost, which of course would necessitate the behemoth being killed and the Mask being kept busy long enough for the ghost to rise. This was the fight that included someone\u2019s character getting picked up and thrown into the stratosphere, then falling down and perfect-dodging the ground, so the entire world moved out of their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T02:08:31-08:00","id":1372237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369936-what-unique-weaknesses-did-you-give-your-deathlords?p=1372081#post1372081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ignoring broken Elder Charms from the 1st release of Dreams of the First Age, I thought Deathlords were epic but approachable antagonists in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> If I understood them correctly, they were intelligent &amp; cunning antagonists whom can learn from past defeats, had massive resources, &amp; not the type you want to fight more than once. I thought that gave a secret weakness that can kept them defeated a distinct appeal, regardless if you curb stomped them once or not.<br /> <br /> I honestly can not think of any antagonists in 2nd Edition that could definitively defeat a Solar Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deprnds on the Solar circle. The stronger Deathlords were Essence 10 guys with every Solar and Abyssal charm.<br /> Walker in Darkness killed my group's essence 5 Full Moon in one round. They only defeated him by using Singular Rune of Hate 3 times (the Solar spell that causes you to lose a dot of every ability and attribute, and a dot of essence, so they basically screwed their own characters permanently).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}